  "title": "Bryce Canyon Hike",
  "indexDescription": "Bryce Canyon family hike in 2002.",
  "description": "As part of our family trip to the Southwest we visited Bryce Canyon National Park and hiked down into it.\n\nBryce Canyon National Park is much smaller and is at a higher elevation than Zion National Park.  Bryce, Zion and the Grand Canyon stair step each other. The bottom elevation of Bryce is the top elevation of Zion and the bottom of Zion is the top of the Grand Canyon.\n\nThe rim at Bryce is about 8,000 feet.",
